<section class="section section--text bg-cream-tint" id="process">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head scroll-reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">The process</p>
      <h2>From first inquiry to residency card.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Applications are filed with Panama's National Immigration Service. Processing is 30 to 90 days from document submission to provisional permit. A short in-country trip is typically required for biometrics.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="home-steps scroll-reveal" data-reveal="stagger">
      <li>Consultation: a 15-minute assessment call to confirm eligibility and preferred route.</li>
      <li>Documents: passport, apostilled background check, bank reference, solvency proof, health certificate, and photos.</li>
      <li>Investment: execute the qualifying real estate, securities, or bank-deposit route.</li>
      <li>Filing: the complete package is filed with Servicio Nacional de Migración.</li>
      <li>Biometrics: a short Panama trip for fingerprints and a provisional permit.</li>
      <li>Card: the permanent residency card is issued; there is no renewal requirement.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="section-more">
      <a class="cta-link cta-link--ink" href="/panama-qualified-investor-visa-process-2026">
        See the full process
      </a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

